        ['Explain what fair use and Creative Commons are and how pupils should use other people\'s images in a presentation.', ['Fair use', 'Creative Commons', 'Credit', 'Permission'], 'Fair use allows limited use of copyrighted work for study or criticism with credit. Creative Commons licences let creators allow reuse under conditions such as giving credit. Pupils should use images with suitable licences, credit the creator and source, and avoid using whole works without permission.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 5],
        ['Suggest four ways to maintain digital wellbeing.', ['Four sensible ways'], 'Set limits on screen time, keep phones away at bedtime, take regular breaks and exercise, turn off unnecessary notifications, and spend time with family and friends offline.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 4],
        ['A classmate shares a fake, embarrassing picture of you in a group chat. Describe what you should do.', ['Stay calm', 'Evidence', 'Report/block', 'Tell an adult'], 'Do not reply angrily or retaliate. Take screenshots as evidence. Ask the group admin to remove it and report or block the person. Tell a parent, teacher or counsellor; serious cases can be reported to the platform and authorities.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 4],
