        ['Explain the four main objects in Microsoft Access and the purpose of each.', ['Tables', 'Forms', 'Queries', 'Reports'], 'Tables store the data in rows (records) and columns (fields). Forms provide a friendly screen to enter and view records. Queries find, filter, sort and calculate data from tables. Reports present data in a formatted layout for printing, with grouping and totals.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 8],
